## World State architecture delivered

Process-global overlay maps are no longer the write authority. Session-scoped `WorldState` owns persistent world data; façades and workers use that boundary.

### Authority (`world/world_state.gd`)
- Owns terrain / feature / channel storage
- Domain revisions: terrain, feature, feature-tile, channel + global
- `mesh_input_revision` for worker invalidation
- Batch transactions (`begin_batch` / `end_batch`)
- `changed(domain, revision)` event stream
- Session `replace_active` / `reset_*`
- Immutable snapshots + `restore_overlay_snapshot` (rollback)
- Save `export_save_overlays` / `apply_save_overlay_dicts`

### Compatibility façades
`TerrainEdits`, `FeatureRegistry`, `ChannelRegistry` keep the same public APIs but delegate all storage/mutations to the active `WorldState`. Plant denial caches are derived-only and cleared on session change.

### Workers
- `ChunkData.capture_worker_snapshot()` freezes mesh-input overlays from `WorldState` and stamps `overlay_mesh_stamp`
- `ChunkManager.is_mesh_job_stale()` rejects token **or** mesh-stamp supersession and rebuilds

### Save
`SaveGameService` reads/writes overlays through `WorldState` while keeping the existing JSON schema fields.

