The objective is NOT to add gameplay.

The objective is to make Crystal Storm feel smooth while preserving all existing gameplay.

Player experience is measured by:

* Stable frame rate
* Smooth chunk streaming
* No noticeable freezes
* Low input latency
* Consistent frame pacing

NOT by adding new content.

---

## Engine Status

Engine 1.0 is frozen.

Do not redesign:

* WorldState
* Chunk Pipeline
* Save Architecture
* Composition Root
* Spatial Query Layer
* Crystal Simulation

Do not remove systems.

Do not simplify gameplay.

Do not reduce world size.

Do not lower visual quality simply to increase FPS.

Engine modifications are allowed only when required to eliminate a measured bottleneck.

---

## Performance Philosophy

Never optimize blindly.

Never guess.

Never assume.

Every optimization must begin with evidence.

Every optimization must end with measurements proving improvement.

If you cannot measure a bottleneck, do not modify it.

---

## First Objective

Build a permanent runtime profiling system.

The game must expose frame timing for every major subsystem.

Example:

