Worker Pool

* Active Workers
* Queue Depth
* Average Job Time
* Longest Job

The profiler must make bottlenecks obvious during gameplay.

---

## Streaming Requirements

Chunk streaming must become invisible.

Measure:

* chunk generation time
* mesh build time
* mesh upload time
* main-thread stalls
* worker utilization
* queue depth
* chunk lifetime
* rebuild frequency

If frame spikes occur, determine exactly which stage caused them.

---

## Runtime Budgets

Treat these as engineering targets.

Frame budget:
16.6 ms (60 FPS)

Chunk generation:
<10 ms average

Mesh upload:
No visible hitching

Main thread stalls:
<2 ms whenever possible

Worker utilization:
High

Queue depth:
Stable

No subsystem may monopolize a frame.

---

## Required Workflow

For every optimization:

1. Measure.
2. Identify the hottest subsystem.
3. Optimize only that subsystem.
4. Re-measure.
5. Compare before/after.
6. Verify gameplay remains unchanged.
7. Document the improvement.

Never perform broad refactors.

Prefer small, measurable improvements.

---

## Acceptable Optimizations

✓ Mesh generation

✓ Worker scheduling

✓ Memory allocation

✓ Object pooling

✓ Chunk caching

✓ Dirty-region rebuilding

✓ Render batching

✓ Mesh upload reduction

✓ Sleeping AI

✓ Update throttling

✓ Spatial query efficiency

✓ Save/load efficiency

✓ Streaming prioritization

✓ Allocation reduction

✓ Cache locality

---

## Unacceptable Optimizations

✗ Removing gameplay

✗ Removing biomes

✗ Reducing world size

✗ Disabling systems

✗ Breaking determinism

✗ Skipping verification

✗ Guess-based optimization

✗ Massive architecture rewrites

---

## Verification

Do not run the complete verification suite after every optimization.

Instead:

1. Run only the verification relevant to the modified subsystem.

2. Launch the playable game.

3. Profile runtime performance.

4. Confirm the hitch or slowdown is improved.

Only run the full verification suite before declaring the milestone complete.

---

## Success Criteria

This milestone is complete only when:

* Walking across the world feels smooth.
* Chunk loading no longer causes noticeable freezes.
* Frame pacing is stable.
* Worker threads remain busy without overwhelming the main thread.
* The runtime profiler clearly identifies where frame time is spent.
* Existing gameplay behaves identically before and after optimization.

Do not add new gameplay during this milestone.

The only deliverable is a faster, smoother Crystal Storm.

At the end of the milestone provide:

* Before vs. after frame timings
* Largest bottleneck discovered
* Largest improvement achieved
* Remaining top three performance issues
* Exactly one recommendation for the next optimization milestone


